Z||000000||Axmanmkii||12-28-2001||12:38 PM||||Browsing through this forum some more, seeing all your guys Fiero just made me fell in love with the car!<P>So how long did it took to get your car to the way it is? <P>I also notice the diffrent body shape, which weird since the car only been out for 4 years. But which year have the smooth curve hmmmm....hood....trunk....hatch? Whatever you call it, and which year have the verticle dropoff thingy? You know what I mean?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||12-28-2001||12:53 PM||||Let me help sort a few items out here... the only body items that are really different are as follows:  Front Fascia (nose) avaialable in early coupe (84-86), late coupe (87-88), and "Aero" (84 Indy, 85 GT, 86-88GT).  The Rear Fascia (lower bumper) also available in the same sets as front fascia.  The Lower rocker panels (lower door & below) available in plain (nothing) and "Aero" (trim... like GTs). The most recognizable panel, the "Sail Panel" available in "Notchback" (used on coupes, indy, formula, and 85 GTs), and "Fastback" (used on all 86-88GTs).  With the fastback also came changes in deck lid (rear trunk) and taillight assemblies.<P>That's about as basic as I think I can go   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Welcome BTW!<P>Edit: Oh yeah... I've been working on my car for 7 years now.  And I've got a load of body mods planned for next year too!<P>------------------<BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 12-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Axmanmkii||12-28-2001||01:06 PM||||uuuuuhhhhh.....<P>What?<P>Sorry, but I'm more of a visual guy...||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||12-28-2001||01:13 PM||||MinnGreen has a GT fastback 86 1/2+<BR>I have an 86 SE which is called a notchback, but in 85 the GT looked like mine.  Both have the aero nose.<P>The base models have the pointy nose and the notchback.<P>You'll figure it out!<P>------------------<BR>Its never going to be finished...<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig2_2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 12-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Smoooooth GT||12-28-2001||01:23 PM||||Welcome to the forum!!! There are many different thing's that you can do to the Fiero.. It all depend's on what YOU want.. I decided to be different with mine and totally redo the body "without" a bodykit!! I've been working on mine for 13 month's.. Mine started out as a notchback..  Good luck with whatever you decide to do!! Steve<BR>here's a pic...  sorry it's just of part of the car!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/008_10.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooooothgtsig_9.gif">                           <BR><A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A>   <BR>Technical  Support (903) 825-7744 Steve<P>"Smoooooth GT"<BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, side scoop's, sail scoop's, ZR-1 hood scoop, decklid scoop, BMW Z~3 vent's, 308 headlight cover's, Custom front and rear fascia's...smooooth!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||REDHOTT88||12-28-2001||01:26 PM||||The white car in the upper right hand side of the forum page(with Santa in it) is a GT model.  So is the red car over to the left of page. (Smooth as you say)<P>The silver car on the left on the "mall" page  and the black car just above my post, Joe Torma, is "notchback" or ("drop off thingy" as you called it.) Although his is upgraded..<P>Both cars start off the same, the notchback can be made into the GT body style with a few bolt on parts.<P>Go to the top of page and find "Fiero gallery", lots of pics.<P><BR>------------------<BR>                                                                                                         <BR>                <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/FIREdevil.gif">      <FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> <B>1988 Formula 2.8L V6</B> 5 speed Getrag </FONT><BR>            <I><FONT SIZE="1">(Runs smooth, shifts crisp, goes fast, red and shiny all over!)</FONT></I><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-28-2001).]||||reg||12
