Z||000007||MinnGreenGT||12-28-2001||01:35 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>MinnGreen has a GT fastback 86 1/2+<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>*Cough* <B>87</B>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Ok... here's a pic of my old '84SE (yes- it was a beater).<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Robs84se01.jpg">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Robs84se05.jpg">  <BR>Notice it has "pads" on the front & rear bumpers. These are the "early coupe" bumpers<P>Now here is my 87GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/greenrear1.jpg">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">  <BR>Now notice the "Aero" Trim used on all GT's and some SE's... The sloped nose, and the more rounded rear end.<P>Also compare the "Sail Panel" (upper-rear body panel) and you'll see thee difference between the "fastback" and the "notchback".<P>Finally, here's a photo of a late model coupe (88 I think) with the more rounded front & rear fascias (still a notchback)<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/gallery/Cars/Fiero_1.jpg">  <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/gallery/Cars/Fiero_2.jpg">  <P>Does it make more sense now?<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 12-28-2001).]||||reg||1
