Z||000010||Oreif||12-28-2001||03:32 PM||||The car was made for 5 years not 4.<BR>1984<BR>only 2 body styles available coupe and Aero Notchback. The ONLY car to have the Aero body was the Indy Pace Car. (only about 2000 made) All cars had 4-cyl. Option packages were base coupe and SE. The SE's had better suspension and upgraded options.<P>1985<BR>2 body styles. Coupe and Aero Notchback.<BR>Aero was only the GT (First year of GT's)<BR>V-6's came out this year also. V-6's were standard on the GT optional on the SE.<P>1986<BR>3 body styles. Coupe, Aero Notchback and Fastback. Fastbacks were only GT's. Aero's were only SE's. The GT's had V-6's the SE came with 4-cyl's but had the V-6 as an option. They looked the same as an 85 GT but the lower trim was painted black where on GT's (all of them up to 87) had silver.<BR>The 86 GT is sometimes referred to as an 86 1/2 because it came out late in the model year.<P>1987<BR>3 body styles, same as 86. The nose and rear of the coupes changed to a smoother look. This was the only year Blue was offered for paint.<P>1988<BR>2 body styles. The coupe and the fastback GT. They dropped the aero notchback. The coupes had a version called a Formula. It was basically a GT with a coupe body. It had the V-6 and the 15" lace style wheels. 88's also had major design changes in the suspension and brakes. The 15" lace wheels have a different offset from front to rear. You can see the difference in the lip on the outside edge of the wheels. Yellow was an 88 only color too. Finally the GT's had 1 color paint. (They did not have the lower moldings painted silver)<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
